; form-glass-organs-live.fk — the organs process: every organ gives into the glass.
; preflight-exec: forbidden
;
; One kernel, no forks, no scans, no files: every 500 ms it reads the sequence
; of every frame that stands (the sensor frames and every publisher in the live
; telemetry space), runs the surprise organ over each channel's give rate, routes
; each surprise through attuned-inquiry as a choice point with a validated
; choice receipt, names each channel's protocol and the cell grammar it carries,
; and gives ONE snapshot into the `organs` frame. The glass reads that frame like
; any other publisher; the events (e) and channels (c) views render its rows,
; each with the shared-memory name and the sequence it was read at.
;
; An idle organ gives idle rows under the frame's own sequence; nothing is sampled.
; The logic lives in form/form-stdlib/form-glass-organs.bml; this file is the carrier.
;
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/form-glass-live.bml form/form-stdlib/form-glass-organs.bml

(fgor-loop (FGLRoot) (fgor-state-empty))
